{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "_comment": "Region slices (Rods FEAT-090, owner rule 2026-09-24: split only a region whose full download - road + routing + map z0-14 - is over 2,000 MB, along natural sub-regions, into the fewest pieces of at most 2,000 MB). The FINAL list (Tadas 2026-09-24: 12 regions -> 36 pieces; GB = 2 pieces). Read by region-slices-pilot.yml (road data + routing, pilot prerelease only) and by basemap-tiles.yml (production map files: a split country ships one map file per piece, never a whole-country file). Every stored outline is REPARTITIONED by build-slice-polys.py (land stays with its admin units, sea and leftovers go to the nearest land; `land` = the admin units whose land counts when the extract is not a whole country, default the country's Natural Earth admin-0). Never read by the monthly osm-extract / valhalla-tiles runs. Japan, Indonesia, Norway, Australia, Mexico and Brazil-Sudeste were added 2026-09-25 (FEAT-090 L4) from the phase-2 piece names; their routing slices are not built yet. sources = Geofabrik paths (no -latest.osm.pbf) whose dated extracts make the piece's road data; outline = how scripts/build-slice-polys.py derives the stored scripts/polys/<id>.poly (every piece has one, so map, routing and app read the same repartitioned file); clipRoadData = cut the merged sources to the outline (needed when the outline is smaller than its sources); mapMaxZoom defaults to 14.",
  "capMb": 2000,
